# oc-sim scenario v1
# RATCHET's input submenu (journal/D-035): launch it from the app menu as in
# ratchet.scn, click the right encoder on COUNT to open its submenu, pick CV2
# (two detents), move CV2 between 1 V and 3 V, then go to SCALE (one detent
# of the left encoder) and set it to x0.50. The snapshot shows the submenu, a
# frame over the main screen: COUNT and the count a burst would take now
# (4 + 4 x (2.5 V x 0.50) = 9) in its top edge; CV2, the scale x0.50 in a lit
# box, the shift; MIN and MAX at their defaults; EFFECT ADD; the CV bar, the
# signal once scaled, 1.25 V, as a band from 0 V and a block, the reading,
# 2.5 V, a stroke, the range seen (0 V on opening to 3 V) a line on top; the VAL
# bar, the panel's 4 a tick and 9 a block; under the frame, the bottom of the
# timeline.
ticks 320
20  button up down
60  button down down
70  button up up
70  button down up
90  button down down
100 button down up
110 button down down
120 button down up
130 button down down
140 button down up
160 button right down
166 button right up
200 button right down
206 button right up
230 encoder 2 +2
240 cv 2 1000
250 cv 2 3000
260 cv 2 2500
270 encoder 1 +1
280 encoder 2 -10
